# Drop out - a bar of silence before the new track arrives.
#
# The whole mix is taken away for a moment. On a floor it reads as a mistake for about half
# a second and then as intent, which is exactly the effect; on headphones it is a breath.
# Short by design - the gap is an eighth of the span, so a couple of seconds at most.

name    Drop out
note    takes everything away for a moment, then the new track lands
bars    8
align   beat
tempo   free
power   free

lane out gain
    bar 0    1.0    hold
    bar 3    1.0    smooth
    bar 4    0.0    hold
    bar 8    0.0    hold

lane out lowpass
    bar 2   16000   smooth
    bar 4     250   hold
    bar 8     250   hold

# Nothing at all for a bar, then in.
lane in gain
    bar 0    0.0    hold
    bar 5    0.0    hold
    bar 8    1.0    hold

lane in bass
    bar 0    -40    hold
    bar 5      0    hold
    bar 8      0    hold

hook bar 4   toast ...
